Z||000000||fiero56||05-14-2000||01:17 AM||||A few weeks ago, I bought a pair of the factory "trumpet" exhaust tips(factory on some Fieros) at Ed's swap meet from mrfiero. They weren't in "brand new" shape. They were pretty dirty, with those little bumps all over that chrome gets over time. Well, I finally got a chance to work on them Friday, and they look AWSOME! It took me about 20 minutes to make the pair look brand new again. Gone are the little bumps, scratches, horrible dirt, and heat discoloration. The best stuff I have found for cleaning any shiny metal is "Mothers Mag and Aluminum Polish." These tips look great. I can't wait to have them installed. Hopefully it shines up my deck release solonoid this well.||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-14-2000||02:36 PM||||I tried Mothers too, and it gives you some awesome results if you take some time with it.  I polished some portions of my motor and wheels.  Looks like a million bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||05-14-2000||10:01 PM||||If you guys enjoyed the mothers polishing stuff you'd be amazed at the autosol product.  It give the same results in half the time....<P>Later||||reg||1
